END-TO-END AIOps ALERT PIPELINE — FINAL WORKING STEPS
 PHASE 1 — VM Setup
 Create Two VMs
VM	Purpose	Region
target-vm	Generates metrics via Node Exporter	asia-southeast1-a
monitoring-vm	Runs Prometheus + Alertmanager + Flask AI engine	asia-southeast1-a
 PHASE 2 — Setup TARGET VM (Metrics Source)
SSH into target-vm:
gcloud compute ssh target-vm --zone=asia-southeast1-a

Install Node Exporter:
sudo apt update -y
wget https://github.com/prometheus/node_exporter/releases/download/v1.6.1/node_exporter-1.6.1.linux-amd64.tar.gz
tar xvf node_exporter-1.6.1.linux-amd64.tar.gz
cd node_exporter-1.6.1.linux-amd64
./node_exporter &

Verify:

Open:

http://<target-vm-external-ip>:9100/metrics

 PHASE 3 — Setup MONITORING VM
SSH:
gcloud compute ssh monitoring-vm --zone=asia-southeast1-a

Install Docker + Compose:
sudo apt update -y
sudo apt install -y docker.io docker-compose
sudo systemctl enable docker
sudo systemctl start docker

Create monitoring folder:
mkdir -p ~/monitoring
cd ~/monitoring

 PHASE 4 — Prometheus Configuration
Create prometheus.yml:
cat > ~/monitoring/prometheus.yml << 'EOF'
global:
  scrape_interval: 15s

scrape_configs:
  - job_name: 'node_exporter'
    static_configs:
      - targets: ['34.124.231.170:9100']
EOF

 PHASE 5 — Alert Rules
Create alert_rules.yml:
cat > ~/monitoring/alert_rules.yml << 'EOF'
groups:
- name: node_alerts
  rules:
  - alert: NodeExporterDown
    expr: up{job="node_exporter"} == 0
    for: 1m
    labels:
      severity: critical
    annotations:
      summary: "Node Exporter Down"
      description: "The Node Exporter on {{ $labels.instance }} is down."
EOF

 PHASE 6 — Alertmanager Configuration
Create alertmanager.yml:
cat > ~/monitoring/alertmanager.yml << 'EOF'
global:
  resolve_timeout: 5m

route:
  receiver: aiops-bot

receivers:
  - name: aiops-bot
    webhook_configs:
      - url: 'http://10.148.0.3:5000/alert'
EOF


 10.148.0.3 is monitoring-vm internal IP.


 PHASE 7 — Run Prometheus + Alertmanager
Run Prometheus:
sudo docker run -d --name prometheus \
  --network host \
  -v ~/monitoring/prometheus.yml:/etc/prometheus/prometheus.yml \
  -v ~/monitoring/alert_rules.yml:/etc/prometheus/alert_rules.yml \
  prom/prometheus

Run Alertmanager:
sudo docker run -d --name alertmanager \
  --network host \
  -v ~/monitoring/alertmanager.yml:/etc/alertmanager/alertmanager.yml \
  prom/alertmanager \
  --config.file=/etc/alertmanager/alertmanager.yml

 PHASE 8 — Flask AI Webhook Service
Create Python file:
nano ~/monitoring/ai_anomaly_insights.py


Paste:

from flask import Flask, request, jsonify
import requests, json

app = Flask(__name__)

SLACK_WEBHOOK_URL = "https://hooks.slack.com/services/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"

@app.route('/alert', methods=['POST'])
def alert_handler():
    data = request.json
    print("Received Alert:", data)

    message = f"*Prometheus Alert Triggered!*\n```{json.dumps(data, indent=2)}```"
    requests.post(SLACK_WEBHOOK_URL, json={"text": message})
    
    return jsonify({"status": "received"})

if __name__ == '__main__':
    app.run(host='0.0.0.0', port=5000)

